ing processes, and risk-management records, integrated into our existing Git-based workflows.\",\n\"why\": \"It converts a compliance obligation into an internal knowledge asset that accelerates new-researcher onboarding and streamlines the rapid scope-justification demands of each funding cycle.\"\n},\n{\n\"title\": \"Compliance Gate Before Any Model Deployment\",\n\"what\": \"Introduce a brief structured checkpoint in our existing project-review cadence where each high-risk system's logging and traceability design is assessed before it enters the testing phase.\",\n\"how\": \"Add a half-day review panel of two engineers and one legal liaison drawn from our small compliance budget, checking whether the system technically enables the automatic recording events specified in Article 12(2).\",\n\"why\": \"A single early gate avoids expensive late-stage rework, keeping engineering hours on scientific objectives rather than emergency patching when a funder or regulator requests traceability evidence.\"\n}\n]\n}",
