e three are genuinely different:\n1. Infrastructure: build the shared middleware (build something new to use in all projects)\n2. Process/Tooling: CI-integrated documentation pipeline (change how docs are maintained, tied to code)\n3. Quality Assurance: a benchmark/test harness that validates logging fidelity across the dev-to-prod transition (measure and verify)\n\nYes, these are three different things: build infrastructure vs. change process/tooling vs. create a verification/measurement mechanism.\n\nLet me finalize my stance reasoning in 3-5 sentences from the Development Engineer perspective focused on technical viability and prototyping speed/quality.\n",
