ts biweekly to map which logging obligations apply to their system and sequence that work alongside sprint goals.\",\n      \"how\": \"I allocate roughly fifteen percent of each participant's FTE to the pod, funded by a modest reallocation within the existing operational line rather than requesting a new budget heading.\",\n      \"why\": \"This keeps traceability decisions embedded where system choices are actually made, preventing the late-stage rework that historically consumes our project slack.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Traceability as a First-Class Design Metric\",\n      \"what\": \"We treat log-compatibility and projected event-recording volume as explicit constraints during system architecture, alongside accuracy and latency, so that logging is designed in rather than bolted on after convergence.\",\n      \"how\": \"Our design-review checklist gains two mandatory fields covering lifetime log-volume projection and the specific minimums applicable under Article 12(3), and no architecture passes peer review until both are filled in.\",\n      \"why\": \"This front-loads compliance reasoning into the phase where our analysts already concentrate their effort, avoiding a second full redesign cycle later in the project timeline.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
