        "content": "{\n\"reasoning\": \"As Compliance Officer, I read Article 12 as an operational architecture mandate that must be resolved at design time rather than retrofitted after deployment; the lifetime logging obligation means traceability is a first-class technical feature in every high-risk system we ship, not a documentation afterthought. For any biometric verification product in our portfolio falling under Annex III point 1(a), the four specific data-capture fields are hard market-access conditions with no discretion. The 'substantial modification' trigger in paragraph 2(a) further forces us to define, jointly with engineering and legal, exactly what constitutes a change that resets or extends logging obligations before our next release cycle. Failure here exposes the institution to enforcement penalties under the Act's sanction regime and immediate reputational damage in every EU procurement context where our systems are evaluated.\",\n\"stance\": 42,\n\"proposals\": [\n{\n\"title\": \"Mandatory Logging Layer in All High-Risk Pipelines\",\n\"what\": \"A standardized, non-bypassable logging module embedded at the architecture level of every high-risk AI system before it leaves the lab, capturing events relevant to risk identification, substantial modifications, and operational monitoring.\",\n\"how\": \"The engineering teams integrate an event-capture SDK into our standard development framework so that start/end timestamps, input data references, and modification triggers are auto-recorded by default in every sprint deliverable.\",\n\"why\": \"This protects the institution from non-compliance penalties and ensures no system ships without traceability, safeguarding both regulatory standing and market reputation.\"\n},\n{\n\"title\": \"Post-Market Log Surveillance Dashboard\",\n\"what\": \"An internal operations tool that ingests lifetime logs from deployed high-risk systems and flags anomalies relevant to Article 72 post-market monitoring and Article 26