uction Models\",\n\"what\": \"A small internal research track to quantify the latency and memory overhead of Article 12-compliant logging in our flagship high-risk models, producing an open benchmark suite that other labs can reuse.\",\n\"how\": \"Two postdoctoral researchers drawn from our existing computational-linguistics group, with no additional headcount hire, instrument current models with progressively richer logging tiers and publish results as a preprint within two quarters.\",\n\"why\": \"It lets us treat the regulatory constraint as a legitimate research question, generating citable output and external reputation without diverting core algorithmic projects from their timelines.\"\n},\n{\n\"title\": \"Fold Compliance into Sprint Planning as Cross-Cutting Epic\",\n\"what\": \"Rather than carving out a separate compliance budget line, we restructure our quarterly sprint boards so that Article 12 logging requirements appear as acceptance criteria on every high-risk feature ticket from day one.\",\n\"how\": \"I work with our engineering managers to update the development-standard document and run a four-hour workshop per team in month one; no new hires or consultants are needed, just process documentation and a compliance lead drawn from existing staff.\",\n\"why\": \"This keeps our funding allocation transparent to grant reviewers, shows that scientific ambition and regulatory duty are not competing line items, and avoids the cost of retrofitting later.\"\n}\n]\n}",
