, protecting both market access and institutional reputation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Pre-Deployment Logging Compliance Audit Protocol\",\n      \"what\": \"We establish a standing verification regime in which every high-risk release undergoes a structured audit confirming its logs capture all events listed under Article 12(2) and (3), including simulated risk-triggering scenarios that verify logs fire correctly during substantial modifications or emerging-risk situations.\",\n      \"how\": \"A cross-functional team of compliance engineers, data scientists, and QA staff runs quarterly audit cycles using scripted test harnesses that inject edge-case inputs and check resulting log entries against the regulatory checklist, feeding findings into a remediation backlog with 30-day closure SLAs.\",\n      \"why\": \"Catching logging gaps internally before market-surveillance authorities do reduces fine exposure and preserves client trust during contract negotiations.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Lifetime Log-Retention and Documentation Governance\",\n      \"what\": \"We build a governance framework for how logs and associated technical documentation are retained, updated, and made accessible across each system's full operational lifetime per Recital 71, covering retention schedules, auditor access controls, and versioned records of algorithmic or data changes.\",\n      \"how\": \"Compliance drafts a Log-and-Documentation Lifecycle Policy assigning ownership per product line, with automated archival triggers at deprecation dates and semiannual completeness reviews cross-referencing logs against the risk-management file; a designated information officer signs off annually.\",\n      \"why\": \"A clear retention regime lets us demonstrate traceability during regulatory inspections and reassure enterprise buyers that data-governance commitments will hold years after deployment.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
