n period, data-subject fields) a required artifact before any high-risk system project enters active development in our lab.\",\n      \"how\": \"Add the brief as a gate in our existing grant-to-project intake workflow; assign a rotating 0.2 FTE logging reviewer drawn from the platform team rather than hiring dedicated compliance staff.\",\n      \"why\": \"Prevents late-stage retrofitting that historically costs three to five times more than front-loaded design, protecting both project timeline and budget.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Open-Source Reference Logger for Annex III Systems\",\n      \"what\": \"Build a small open-source library implementing Article 12 logging schemas for the most common high-risk categories we serve, reducing per-project compliance engineering and establishing our lab as an implementation reference.\",\n      \"how\": \"Dedicate two senior engineers for one quarter to develop and document the library; release under an EU-friendly licence and present at a standards forum to align with CEN-CENELEC harmonised specifications.\",\n      \"why\": \"Converts a mandatory overhead into a reusable asset that lowers marginal cost on every subsequent project while strengthening our position in public-sector tenders.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
