ery current and future system cuts per-project cost dramatically and protects our limited R&D budget from repeated one-off builds.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Turn Audit Logs into Monitoring Products\",\n      \"what\": \"Redirect a portion of applied research toward tooling that consumes Article 12 logs to detect drift, flag risk events under Article 79(1), and generate the post-market monitoring reports required by Article 72.\",\n      \"how\": \"We would repurpose two existing NLP/ML research teams currently on exploratory grants to build anomaly-detection models over structured log streams, pairing them with the Compliance Officer's audit findings as labelled training data.\",\n      \"why\": \"Converting a mandatory cost centre into a marketable monitoring service offsets compliance spending and gives us a differentiated offering that competitors treating logging as pure overhead cannot easily replicate.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Logging Readiness Gate in Project Lifecycle\",\n      \"what\": \"A mandatory checkpoint before any high-risk system exits the lab, verifying that all Article 12(3) fields are captured, retrievable, and retained for the system's full operational lifetime.\",\n      \"how\": \"I would embed this as a sign-off step in our existing project-review board process, staffed by one compliance engineer and one systems architect who jointly validate log completeness against a written checklist derived directly from the regulation text.\",\n      \"why\": \"Catching gaps at the prototype-to-deployment boundary is orders of magnitude cheaper than retrofitting after market surveillance discovers the deficiency, preserving both institutional reputation and remediation budget for actual R&D.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
