ifecycle Traceability and Documentation Protocol\",\n\"what\": \"A new internal governance procedure requiring every high-risk AI project to maintain a living technical-documentation file covering algorithms, training-data provenance, validation processes, and risk-management decisions, updated at each milestone and retained for the system's full lifetime.\",\n\"how\": \"The compliance function issues a mandatory template aligned with Recital 71, assigns a named documentation owner per project, and embeds documentation-update checkpoints into sprint reviews so gaps are caught before release rather than discovered by a market-surveillance authority.\",\n\"why\": \"Current technical documentation is the evidence base regulators will demand during conformity assessment and post-market monitoring, protecting our reputation and averting enforcement action.\"\n},\n{\n\"title\": \"Post-Market Monitoring Dashboard as Client Feature\",\n\"what\": \"Develop a client-accessible analytics dashboard that surfaces Article 12 logs—usage periods, matched inputs, verification records—in real time, giving downstream deployers the transparency they need to meet their own obligations under Articles 72 and 26(5).\",\n\"how\": \"The product team packages the existing logging layer into an API with a lightweight web front-end, co-designs the interface with two anchor customers during a six-week pilot, and documents the output as part of the conformity-assessment evidence pack.\",\n\"why\": \"Turning a compliance obligation into a value-added feature strengthens our market position, builds client trust, and differentiates us from competitors still treating logging as a back-office cost.\"\n}\n]\n}",
