icle 12 log fields our existing monitoring already captures versus which are genuinely missing.\",\n      \"how\": \"One compliance liaison per project team runs a checklist against the four mandated data points and reports gaps to a single tracker I review weekly until closure.\",\n      \"why\": \"We direct scarce engineering hours only at genuine gaps rather than speculative rebuilds, protecting research FTEs from being silently absorbed by redundant tooling work.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Mandatory Logging Line in Project Charters\",\n      \"what\": \"A governance change requiring every high-risk project charter and grant application to include an explicit budget line—staff-hours, storage, maintenance—for lifetime logging compliance from the design phase onward.\",\n      \"how\": \"I add three fields to our one-page intake form covering logging architecture, retention strategy, and estimated annual ops cost; the funding committee rejects proposals that omit them.\",\n      \"why\": \"Surfacing compliance cost at proposal stage prevents mid-project budget shocks and lets me allocate the lab's constrained funds with full information rather than absorbing surprises later.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
