rs and ensures no system ships without Article 12(1)'s technical capability already embedded in its runtime.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Reference Biometric-Verification Prototype with Mandated Log Fields\",\n      \"what\": \"A working end-to-end prototype of an Annex III point 1(a) biometric identification system that demonstrates capture and persistence of all four Article 12(3) data fields in a live operational loop.\",\n      \"how\": \"Build a minimal but complete pipeline (enrolment, matching, human verification step) where each stage emits structured logs to a queryable store; the verifier-identity field under Article 14(5) is captured via an authenticated session token rather than manual entry.\",\n      \"why\": \"It proves technical feasibility of the four mandated fields in one concrete artifact we can reuse as a template for any future biometric project and present during conformity assessment.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"CI Gate for Log-Schema Compliance Before Deployment\",\n      \"what\": \"An automated pipeline check that validates every high-risk system build emits all required log fields in the correct schema before it is allowed to proceed past pre-production staging.\",\n      \"how\": \"Define a machine-readable log contract (JSON Schema or protobuf) encoding the Article 12(3) minimums plus project-specific events; add a CI step that runs a synthetic workload against the candidate build and asserts every required field appears in emitted logs with valid values.\",\n      \"why\": \"Catches missing or malformed logging at integration time rather than during post-deployment audits, protecting both regulatory compliance and our reputation for shipping production-grade systems on schedule.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
